/* Rear camera CSI-2 graph — S5K3L8 -> CSIPHY0 -> (CSID0) on ugglite.
 *
 * Scope: an incremental DT fragment applied on top of the ACCEPTED baseline
 * boot image build/hermes-sensor-candidate/image/ugglite-rear-probe-dt-boot.img
 * (sha256 1d443c8c0894a5bdfd337a9a19dba142dbbf146543418a28fad87e2aeaf15769).
 * The probe node (rails, MCLK, reset, sensor address) already exists there and
 * is NOT redefined here; this fragment adds only the media graph endpoints.
 *
 * Binding facts this fragment rests on (pinned kernel 50f9719b10cef7924…,
 * local copies in build/hardware-next/ and build/hermes-camera-stream/refs/):
 *
 *  1. camss.c:4700-4750 camss_parse_endpoint_node()
 *       - iterates the CAMSS node's own ports; vep.base.port selects the
 *         CSIPHY instance (port@0 -> csiphy0);
 *       - reads data-lanes (num_data_lanes, per-lane position) and
 *         clock-lanes (clock_lane) from that endpoint;
 *       - rejects any bus type other than V4L2_MBUS_CSI2_DPHY.
 *     There is no DT node for CSID/ISPIF/VFE: camss_register_entities() creates
 *     those links in software (csid_link_setup() copies lane_cfg from the
 *     CSIPHY subdevice, camss-csid.c:1256-1280, and builds the CSID lane
 *     assignment from the same data-lane positions, camss-csid.c:1223-1231).
 *     Therefore exactly one endpoint pair is needed: sensor <-> csiphy0.
 *     Adding csid/ispif/vfe nodes in DT would invent nodes the driver does not
 *     look for.
 *
 *  2. v4l2-fwnode.c:209-249 (__v4l2_fwnode_endpoint_parse)
 *       - bus-type is optional: with data-lanes present and the media bus type
 *         unknown, the parser sets V4L2_MBUS_CSI2_DPHY itself (line 229-239),
 *         so camss accepts the endpoint without a bus-type property;
 *         the s5k2xx driver in turn presets .bus_type = CSI2_DPHY explicitly
 *         (s5k2xx.c:1517-1520) and only validates num_data_lanes.
 *       - clock-lanes = <7> follows the settled upstream Qualcomm convention
 *         for CSIPHY endpoints (pinned tree example: sm8250 xiaomi-pipa patch,
 *         csiphy1_ep with clock-lanes = <7>, data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>). The value
 *         lies outside the data-lane bit range 0..3, so the copybook parser
 *         sees no duplicate lane: with clock-lanes absent it would silently
 *         keep clock_lane = 0, colliding with data lane 0.
 *       - physical meaning on msm8917: both csiphy hw_ops variants
 *         (csiphy_get_lane_mask, camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c:994 / -2ph-1-0.c:30)
 *         build the lane-enable mask from data-lane positions plus a FIXED
 *         clock-lane enable bit; lane_cfg.clk.pos is parsed and stored
 *         (camss.c:4733) but never consumed for this SoC. So clock-lanes
 *         documents the link, it does not re-route hardware.
 *
 *  3. data-lanes = <0 1 2 3> is not a guess about board wiring:
 *       - s5k2xx.c:19  S5K2XX_DATA_LANES = 4, and s5k2xx_check_hwcfg()
 *         (s5k2xx.c:1512-1552) refuses the device unless the endpoint declares
 *         exactly 4 data lanes;
 *       - the sensor is a 4-lane part in both S5K3L8 driver modes
 *         (s5k3l8_modes[]: 4208x3120@30 and 1280x720@120, both 562 MHz link
 *         frequency -> pixel_rate = 562e6*2*4 = 4.496 Gbps);
 *       - lane position 0..3 with lane 0 as the first data lane is the
 *         mainline default when positions are not remapped; no pinned vendor
 *         source for ugglite states a swapped polarity or lane order
 *         (vendor dtsi carries camera power/CCI only, camera HAL holds the
 *         rest). A physical swap is therefore NOT claimed here: if the module
 *         really swaps lanes the symptom is a corrupted/failed first frame,
 *         which is exactly what one bounded capture distinguishes.
 *       - clock-lanes = <7> likewise claims nothing about physical clock lane
 *         routing on this board; it is the parser-level "not a data lane"
 *         marker used by every upstream Qualcomm CSI-2 node.
 *
 *  4. link-frequencies = <562000000> is already in the accepted DTB and is
 *     unchanged; the driver's link_freq_menu_items[] index 0 is 562 MHz and
 *     both S5K3L8 modes use it (s5k2xx.c:67-90, 921-947).
 *
 * What this fragment deliberately does NOT do: no regulator, clock, GPIO,
 * pinctrl, panel or kernel change; no front camera; no CCI/EEPROM access; no
 * test-pattern or capture policy (that is scripts/ugglite-capture-rear.sh).
 *
 * Equivalent delta applied by build/hermes-camera-stream/build-candidate.sh to
 * the decompiled accepted DTB (which has no labels, hence explicit phandles):
 *
 *   &camss ports { port@0 { endpoint { clock-lanes=<7>; data-lanes=<0 1 2 3>;
 *                                       remote-endpoint=<&rear_sensor_ep>; }; }; };
 *   &rear_sensor port { endpoint { clock-lanes=<7>; data-lanes=<0 1 2 3>;
 *                                  link-frequencies=<562000000>;
 *                                  remote-endpoint=<&csiphy0_ep>; }; };
 */
